  "critical_dispositions": {
    "R1245": "Current R1245 needs coordinated retirement only after R2826 preserves qualified := admission and downstream references migrate; withdrawn R1245@29 is not successor.",
    "R2592": "Retire old Operator descriptor; R2826 := allowed-value OR and R2828 :: constraint AND replace old combined semantics. R2810@1 and R2777@1 Draft are superseded, not independent Rules.",
    "R2616": "Retire Operator descriptor-only model authority; first eliminate Current unversioned dependencies and replace with Rule references; preserve Actor/Operator.",
    "R2605": "Retire old // instance selector; replace uses with supported typed selection, not the new // narrowing.",
    "R2610": "Retire old / narrowing declaration; R2811 gives // narrowing and R2812 gives / containment. Coordinate R2475/R2476/R2617 and all affected aliases/references.",
    "R1931": "Existing R1931@19 and Current @18 still need integration with final := value Relation, :: constraint semantics and new path grammar; do not accidentally promote stale body or drop unrelated constraints."
  },
  "source_first_plan": [
    "Complete review of the 49 actual Drafts, R1931, predecessor/successor identity mapping, endpoint domains and precise syntax interpretation.",
    "Prepare checked source lifecycle batch: retire only exact Current predecessors whose replacement or redundancy is established; promote correct Drafts with unique ID/version, archive exact Current predecessors and retarget Current unversioned dependencies. Preserve frozen/versioned references and unrelated business Drafts.",
    "After the reviewed source checkpoint, migrate Current and Draft CFEL syntax in place by parsed context, preserving metadata identities, YAML separators, quoted literals and @version data; recheck subject bindings, counts, directions and source coverage.",
    "Refresh all seven projections against the actual final source frontier; then hand implementation, readers and mandatory runtime/regression gates to CA #3. Source-first sequencing is user-authorized and is not blocked on pre-existing reader compatibility."
  ],
